-- title:
--   Vanishing residue forces divisibility by q for cusp-regular modular functions
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'\ge 1$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the field $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(M')=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the subfield `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $M'$) along $A$, with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ with kernel its maximal ideal, and a map on places, subject to the compatibilities of `ConstantReduction`. Assume $R_0$ reads $q$-expansions coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in the field, that image is $R_0$-integral and its residue, viewed in $(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)((q))$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $g\in\mathbb Q((q))$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, have $R_0$-integral image, satisfy $\mathrm{ord}_P(g)\ge 0$ at every place $P$ of the field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mathrm{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$, and have vanishing $R_0$-residue. Then there is $g'\in\mathbb Q((q))$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, again with $R_0$-integral image and again regular at every place where $j$ is regular, with $g=q\,g'$.
--
--   This identifies the kernel of the coefficientwise (constant) reduction on the $R_0$-integral, cusp-regular modular functions of level $M'$ with rational $q$-expansion as exactly $q$ times that same set; it rests on the integrality statement [`ModularCurve.algebraMap_coeff_mem_of_mem_integers_of_cuspRegular`](thm.html#ModularCurve.algebraMap_coeff_mem_of_mem_integers_of_cuspRegular). It is used in the construction of algebra homomorphisms compatible with residues for the full-level and $\Gamma_1$-type rigid data classifications.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_eq_natCast_mul_of_residue_eq_zero_of_mem_integers_of_cuspRegular.lean

